In summary, driven by the urgent needs and guided by classical crystallization theory, a straightforward, convenient and broad applicable approach for size precisely controlled synthesis of nanoMOFs has been developed. The preciseness of size control and the uniformity of nanoMOFs are ensured by the “controlled nucleation” and the following “controlled growth” in this strategy. Undoubtedly, this approach will facilitate the academic researches on nanoMOFs to achieve better performance in various applications. More importantly, this strategy enables scale-up production of nanoMOFs with precise size control under mild condition in a cost-effective way. The availability of homogeneous nanoMOFs of customized sizes will greatly promote the academia-to-industry transposition of MOFs, especially in biomedicine, catalysis and thin film devices.
